    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. Let me confirm the final response shape end-to-end with a quick check of the audit + identity output already visible in the run: `memberId=V2NSW2716E6609E7`, audit line `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,...}`.\n\nAll green. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity with minimal, localized changes \u2014 each in a small, self-contained unit.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in, every identifier changes):**\n- `OwnerMemberIdPolicy` \u2014 memberId region is now the version-2 region: body prefixed with the `V2` tag \u2192 `V2<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. `V2NSW2716E6609E7`). The Luhn digit recomputes over the new body.\n- `OwnerHouseholdPolicy` \u2014 householdId hashes `\"V2|\" + lastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n- `OwnerIdentityPolicy` \u2014 identityKey hashes `\"V2|\"` prepended to its input.\n\nBecause each derivation is seeded with a `V2` tag that v1 never produced, every identifier changes and no v1 value recurs.\n\n**Plain, user-facing fields stay plain:**\n- `OwnerLocalityPolicy` \u2014 strips the leading `V2` tag before reading the region, so `locality` remains `NSW`. `timezone` (derives from locality) and `OwnerSegmentPolicy`'s area both stay plain, and the owner segment is recomputed from the version-2 memberId. v1/seed memberIds (which never start with `V2`) are unaffected.\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):**\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema; `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` moved off the top level into a nested `identity` object.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`.\n- `OwnerMapper` gets a small `toIdentity(owner)` helper plus `apiVersion` constant and `identity` mappings; the old top-level `identityKey` mapping removed.\n\n**Audit (`OwnerAuditPolicy`):** the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carries `\"schemaVersion\":2`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
