    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. I've split it into what runs *before* the controller body, then each step of the controller in the exact order the code invokes it.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, or the request is rejected (403).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 failures produce 400 with `schemaValidationErrors`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` (must contain **exactly 10 digits**)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraint\n\n## Inside the controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`), in order\n\n3. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`** \u2014 transformations (side-effects on the entity being built):\n   - **address composed/normalized**: trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; prefers `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`) over flat `address`.\n   - **telephone normalized to E.164** (`E164Telephone.toE164`): strips separators, keeps `+CC` or assumes `+61` dropping a leading `0`. During this it calls **`OwnerTelephoneLengthPolicy`** \u2014 validation: `+61` requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10, else 400 (`InvalidNationalNumberLengthException`).\n   - **email lower-cased**.\n\n4. **`OwnerRegistrationDatePolicy.assignBusinessDayRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect*: rejects a future registration date (400); defaults null to today; rolls weekends and hard-coded 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day. **Mutates `registrationDate`.**\n\n5. **`OwnerDailyLimitPolicy.rejectWhenDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 *validation*: if \u2265 **100** existing owners share that registration date \u2192 429.\n\n6. **`OwnerCityCapacityPolicy.rejectWhenCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 *validation*: if \u2265 **50** existing owners in the same city \u2192 409.\n\n7. **`OwnerPostcodePolicy.rejectInvalidPostcode`** \u2014 *validation*: if postcode present and city is a known region (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099), out-of-range \u2192 400. Unknown city or null postcode passes.\n\n8. **`OwnerDisposableEmailPolicy.rejectDisposableDomain`** \u2014 *validation*: email domain in {mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com} \u2192 400.\n\n9. **`OwnerHouseholdPolicy.rejectDuplicateHousehold`** \u2014 *side-effect only* (no longer rejects despite the name): **mutates `householdId`** to a 6-char hash of `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`. The `sharesHousehold` argument is now unused.\n\n10. **`OwnerIdentityPolicy.rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect*: computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 of `V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`; if a non-deleted owner already has that key \u2192 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException`). Otherwise it calls **`OwnerPossibleDuplicatePolicy`**, which **mutates `possibleDuplicateOf`** to a matching owner's id when soundex(lastName)+postcode collides with a different identityKey (soft flag, not a rejection).\n\n11. **`OwnerNamesakePolicy.assignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect*: **mutates `namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n12. **`OwnerMemberIdPolicy.assignMemberId`** \u2014 *side-effect*: **mutates `memberId`** = `V2 + region + 2-digit FY + 8-char hash + Luhn check digit`, de-duplicated against existing member IDs by appending `-<n>`.\n\n13. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional`; persists via Spring Data `save`. On persist, the entity's **`@PrePersist`** fallback sets `registrationDate` to today if still null (already set in step 4). Entity-level Bean Validation also applies here (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, and the entity's own E.164 `@Pattern` on telephone). **No DB unique constraints** exist on any owner column.\n\n14. **`OwnerAuditPolicy.auditCreate`** \u2014 *side-effect (post-save)*: logs two lines to the `AUDIT` logger, including a structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event with an incrementing sequence number.\n\n15. **`OwnerWelcomeNotificationPolicy.enqueueWelcome`** \u2014 *side-effect (post-save)*: logs a line to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n16. **Response assembly** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` derives many response-only fields (telephone display, fiscal year, membership points/level, locality, timezone, warnings, segment, risk flag, self link, etc. \u2014 **none persisted**); sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}`; returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **Idempotency variant**: if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present, `OwnerIdempotentCreateControllerV1` handles the request instead \u2014 a repeated key returns the cached `OwnerDto` with **200** (in-memory map, no eviction); otherwise it delegates to the flow above and caches the result.\n- **No email/telephone *uniqueness* check runs.** `OwnerEmailPolicy`/`OwnerTelephonePolicy` (and their duplicate-exceptions) exist but are **dead code** in the create path \u2014 referenced only by the exception advice. The only duplicate rejection that fires is `OwnerIdentityPolicy` (step 10)."
